cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Adjudicating the viral auxiliary metabolic gene record: disputed families
  cancel in comparisons and persist in descriptions
message: >-
  If you use this software or the analysis in it, please cite the preprint and
  the archived Zenodo release rather than the GitHub URL, which is mutable.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Murphy
    affiliation: Independent researcher, United Kingdom
    email: daniel.s.murphy@outlook.com
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # add once registered
repository-code: 'https://github.com/dmurfy06/amg-annotation-audit'
abstract: >-
  An audit of three published viral auxiliary metabolic gene (AMG) catalogues
  spanning ocean, soil and wastewater. 35 gene families were adjudicated against
  a pre-registered rule with a six-tier evidence hierarchy; 28 survive. The
  exposed portion of the record sits in families the current evidence base
  cannot adjudicate in either direction rather than families shown to be wrong,
  and the effect on published claims is strongly claim-dependent: comparative
  claims are robust, descriptive claims are not.
keywords:
  - bacteriophage
  - auxiliary metabolic genes
  - viromics
  - genome annotation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
doi: '10.5281/zenodo.21876444'
